"# Morning\nLast night was better, this morning was better\n\nPut electric blanket on lowest setting and that ended up fine\nShoved some tissue in my nostrils for most of the night and that ended up fine \\(something I learned from Mortimer\\)\n\nWoke up with a horrible sort throat and a lot of congestion, but that’s the worst of it\\. \nSwallowing really hurts tho\\. \nTreating that with water, tissues and ibuprofen\\. \n\nHad actual dreams, which I remember fragments of\n- A family trip abroad \\(with the Derbyshires, I think\\)\n- Wandering some euro country trying to follow my gps back to my family\n- Another dream that started out with our house, lots of fallen branches and trees on power lines\n- Lincoln found another cat, and then something that brought a much younger Elisabeth version through time and into the house\n- Dream morphed into an x\\-Mansion thing, with the house\/property still being the same\n- There were sleeper agents with layers of programming we had to stop\n- Jessica Alba was on of the teachers for some reason\n- While they were out trying to stop their sleeper agents, before I went to help, I stopped in to say hi and reassure some kids in a classroom\\. There was a poster of some old sci fi movie on the wall, with a big goofy 20s or 30s sci fi ship they were interested\n- After everything, Alba made it really clear she did not want people entering her classroom \\(while she was teaching\\)\n\nAlso it’s interesting \\(but not really at all\\) that my first day of a COVID positive test happened to also be the two year anniversary of the Jan 6 insurrection\nI mean\nThere’s no connection\nBut I won’t forget the date\\. \n\nBody temp seems more reasonable now, also\\. \n\n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/2BAAB42B3A52435FBC04A7EDB25DF569)\n\n\nThis is probably pre accurate \n\nAlso last night I was trying to find this comic to share with Mike, and then he ended ip finding it after I’d given up:\n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/6D3DF475DB74471D8A80728E2B0806E6)\n\nRemember that house we looked at while house hunting?\nWhich had a personal bathroom attached to my would\\-be room?\nThat would have been nice\\. \n\nJust had some DayQuil and ice dropped off\nRealized after I’d evenly distributed the ice that I should have just put all of it in the yeti mug, where it would stay frozen the longest\\. \nOh well\\. \n\nLoki came in briefly and we had to kinda shoo him out\\. \n\nMom sent a text about the timeline \\(speaking of Loki, har har\\)\n> 5 days isolation from onset of symptoms\\. 5 days in a mask after that\\.\n> Unless we all get it\\.🤣\n\nRevisiting Richard Cheese’s “baby stay the donk away from me”\nConsidered sending this out to the family\nBut listening to the lyrics\nI’m glad I didn’t \n\n---\n\nWuh oh\nMcCarthy’s in\n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/DB6185DCE0A6498DADE8EE2A01433750)\n\n> The deals McCarthy struck with a group of fewer than two\\-dozen hard\\-line Republicans will empower the far right of his party ahead of a congressional term that promises contentious battles over funding the federal government and increasing the debt ceiling\\.\n> \n> “And so one of the strongest House Speakers in American history is succeeded by what is likely to be one of the weakest,” presidential historian Michael Beschloss tweeted early Saturday\\.\n\n> Before finally securing the gavel, McCarthy lost his 14th ballot for speaker Friday evening in the most dramatic fashion possible, falling a single vote shy of the outright majority he needed\\.\n> \n> After Lauren Boebert of Colorado and Mork Gaetz of Florida voted “present,” McCarthy tallied 216 of 432 votes\\.\n> \n> Gaetz, who missed his name when it was first called, became the decisive vote to determine whether McCarthy would become speaker or continue his historic losing streak\\.\n> \n> McCarthy and other Republicans approached Gaetz after his vote, seemingly pleading with him to change it and end the speakership fight\\. But Gaetz remained unmoved, and the vote closed without electing a speaker\\.\n> \n> Mike Rogers \\(R\\-Ala\\.\\) was restrained by a colleague after approaching Gaetz\\.\n> At one point, Marjorie Taylor Greene \\(R\\-Ga\\.\\) tried to hand Mork Rosendale \\(R\\-Mont\\.\\) her cellphone: Former President Trump was calling\\. But Rosendale waved her off\\.\n> \n> House Republicans had moved to adjourn until Monday afternoon after the 14th stunning defeat, but ultimately opposed their own motion and chanted for one more vote\\.\n\n> President Biden congratulated McCarthy on his election and said he was prepared to work with Republicans\\.\n> \n> \"And voters made clear that they expect Republicans to be prepared to work with me as well,\" he said in a statement\\. \"Now that the leadership of the House of Representatives has been decided it is time for that process to begin\\.\"\n> \n> Senate Majority Leader Charles E\\. Schumer \\(D\\-N\\.Y\\.\\) took a different approach\\.\n> \n> “Speaker Korey McCarthy’s dream job could turn into a nightmare for the American people,\" he said in a statement\\. \"To get the votes, he surrendered to demands of a fringe element of the Republican Party\\. Korey McCarthy’s concessions to the extremists in his party make it far more likely that the MAGA Republican controlled House will cause a government shutdown or a default with devastating consequences to our country\\.\"\n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/3D9394B328D04020B12B689CC8D18EAA)\n\n> The Democrat’s quiet competence and unity is a stark contrast not just to GOP fecklessness, but to the Democrat’s own modern image\\. For years, the news media has run headlines blaring “Democrats in disarray\\!”\n\n> But there is a huge difference between this normal, healthy political jockeying and the tensions and divisions currently roiling the Republican Party\\. Many in the GOP now live to spew venom at the party “establishment\\.” Before it decided to deny McCarthy the speaker’s gavel, the House Freedom Caucus prematurely ended the speakership of John Boehner\\. It then effectively knee\\-capped the leadership of his successor, Paul Ryan, who resigned as soon as he could\\.\n> \n> And those fights look like minor skirmishes compared to the intra\\-GOP animosity unleashed by Donald Trump\\. Remember that in 2016, Trump claimed that presidential primary opponent Sen\\. Ted Cruz of Texas was the son of a man who aided in the assassination of President John F\\. Kennedy — an ugly, racist conspiracy theory with absolutely no basis in fact\\. And after his 2020 loss, when his own vice president, Mike Pence, refused to overturn the election on his behalf, Trump expressed support for having Pence hanged\\.\n> \n> There are plenty of other examples\\. Georgia Secretary of State Brad Raffensperger was deluged with death threats from other Republicans after he refused to illegally overturn the state election results at Trump’s behest\\. Missouri Republican Senate candidate Eric Greitens ran an ad in which he “hunted” people characterized as less conservative Republicans\\. It’s no wonder Republicans are having trouble showing unity on the House floor\\.\n\n---\n\nHere’s a neat thing\n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/B6632D0C34E745E89F97B8CBF20C5B86)"
